sh every single day or  even multiple times a day allowed  victoria beckham or kylie can easily  rack up our mercury intake very quickly  beyond what's considered safe and even  if we swing the pendulum in the other  direction and consume a strict raw ultra  vegan diet of just like fruits and  vegetables it can also wreak havoc on  our gut from the high amount of fiber  and fodmap foods even something as  essential to life as water can have  dangerous consequences when consumed in  excess as the kidneys can only excrete  about a liter of water per hour and  drinking much more than that can  actually be fatal plus if we're  narrowing down our food choices to a  handful of health foods or even  non-health foods like ultra-processed  foods for example we may also run the  risk of overdoing it on certain  additives like emulsifiers sweeteners  oils preservatives or sugar alcohols all  ingredients that are deemed safe in  normal amounts but possibly less optimal  when they're in one of like five foods  that you eat we also have to consider  what we are not eating when we're  limiting ourselves to a handful of foods  variety is the spice of life and it's  also key to good health so there's a few  major reasons why we know this to be  true it is very difficult to meet all of  our nutritional needs even in the  context of a generally very healthy day  even if we weren't to cut out any  specific foods or types of food groups  it would be very difficult to meet all  of your minute little micros and  antioxidants in the context of a single  day so for example we might get more  lycopene in tomatoes and more  beta-carotene in carrots and if we're  switching things up often enough over  time we will tick all the boxes think of  it like having a piece of paper with  like a bunch of little holes in them  when the paper you add on top monday  through friday is cut with the exact  same holes you're never gonna fill those  holes  you're always going to see through the  paper but if everyday's paper has  different size and shape holes in  different places eventually there'll be  no gaps on the page to see through so  this is why we want to switch things up  whenever we can the goal is not to get  everything in in one day we want to  think about the dietary pattern over  time number two now a varied diet is  also important for diversifying the  bacteria in our microbiome which we know  plays an important role for immunity  digestion heart health and even brain  health thanks to the gut brain  connection therefore limited food  variety can lead to a disruption in the  healthy balance of bacteria in the gut  which can lead to bloating indigestion  gas diarrhea or chronic constipation  dysbiosis has also been associated with  increased visceral fat and increased  risk of digestive disorders like ibs  celiac and colitis as well as an  increased risk of chronic diseases like  diabetes and heart disease so ironically  folks who are restricting their food  variety out of fear of weight gain may  actually be doing themselves a  disservice long term we also know that  not getting enough food variety can  impact the production of digestive  enzymes which can actually exacerbate or  even cause food intolerances so for  instance if you stop eating dairy cold  turkey your body essentially halts the  production of the digestive enzymes  needed to digest dairy and when you  suddenly want like a lick of your kids  ice cream bam you feel like it's so damn  hot milk was a bad choice  this is often why food elimination diets  that are not indicated can become a  self-fulfilling prophecy over time so  now you know what to look for in your  own life to determine if your eating  routine is serving you but how can we  optimize our eating for our mental and  physical health here's my tip take your  structure throw in some simple  variations and add intuition and  flexibility let's take some examples  maybe you enjoy oatmeal for breakfast  because it's easy convenient in